WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.115 --> 00:00:02.880
(bright music)

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.490
- [Narrator] Title 42,
the pandemic-era policy

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.340
that allowed US authorities
to quickly expel migrants

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.250
on public health grounds has expired.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.890
The Biden administration
has deployed 1,500

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:15.990
active duty troops at the southern border

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.250
to assist the border patrol

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.100
with processing as fears
of a significant surge

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.183
of migrants grow.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.420
Wall Street Journal's
Alicia A. Caldwell reports

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:28.170
from El Paso, Texas and
explains what Title 42 is,

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.473
the effect it has had on the
border and what comes next.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:37.320
- Title 42 is a public
health law that was used

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.950
by the Trump administration
to quickly remove

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.230
or expel migrants who
crossed the border illegally,

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.180
intending to ask for asylum.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.670
- [Narrator] The policy's
name comes from Title 42

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:51.840
of the US Legal Code which is
a body of public health laws.

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.870
The Trump administration
began using it in March, 2020

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.640
to turn back migrants on grounds

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.790
that they might bring
COVID-19 into the US.

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.280
Under the policy, most
migrants were sent back

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:05.370
to Mexico after border patrol
agents recorded their names

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.870
and fingerprints.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.300
- Border Patrol and the US
government has been quick

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.120
to point out it was
not an immigration law,

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.670
so it carried with it no
immigration penalties.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.050
- [Narrator] The measure proved to be far

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.180
from an ideal enforcement tool.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.770
It had the unexpected result

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.440
of making it easier
for non-asylum migrants

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.780
to attempt repeated border crossings.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.270
- So if you got caught, got returned,

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.010
you live to see another day in terms

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.860
of your immigration opportunity or chance

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.801
to cross the border illegally
again and make it through.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:35.850
(crowd chatter)

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.460
- [Narrator] Authorities had
already recorded big increases

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.085
in illegal crossings leading
up to Title 42's expiration.

00:01:42.085 --> 00:01:45.720
(crowd chant slogans in foreign language)

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:49.770
In March, cities like El Paso
experienced a 54% increase

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.300
in border patrol encounters,

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.310
compared to the same period last year.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:55.500
Looking at the southwest border overall,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.060
total encounters increased
25% in the same period.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.380
The change in border policy

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.380
has also created confusion among migrants.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.810
- There's tremendous disinformation

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:08.070
and smugglers have an interest

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:11.130
in pushing people across the border now.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:15.630
- I want to be very clear,
our borders are not open.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.210
People who cross our border unlawfully

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.030
and without a legal basis to remain

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:25.050
will be promptly processed and removed.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.570
- [Narrator] The governors of
Arizona and Texas have said

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.390
that the Biden administration's
policies inadequately

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.610
secure the border, leaving them to bear

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.620
the brunt of the migrant waves.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:39.620
- President Biden is
laying down a welcome mat

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.480
to people across the entire world,

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.350
saying that the United
States border is wide open,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.740
and it would lead to an incredible amount

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.230
of people coming across
the border illegally.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.850
- [Narrator] The Secretary
of Homeland Security,

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:56.460
Alejandro Mayorkas said the administration

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.730
is employing a combination
of existing immigration laws

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.961
and a new set of measures to
address the migrant surge.

00:03:02.961 --> 00:03:04.710
(door thuds)

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.890
- People who arrive at our
southern border will be subject

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.470
to our immigration enforcement authorities

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.530
under Title 8 of the United States Code.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.720
- Title 8 is an immigration law

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.520
and does carry penalties.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.650
It is technically a
misdemeanor to cross the border

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.660
without permission and those who do

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.910
and are returned, face a five-year ban

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.770
from returning to the country illegally.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.690
And if they do return and they get caught,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.190
they can face a felony charge
for crossing the border again.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.930
- [Narrator] The Biden
administration's new set

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:38.010
of measures is intended to mimic
the Title 42 border policy.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:40.080
Migrants who enter the US illegally,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.350
which asylum seekers are
allowed to do under current law

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:46.650
will be quickly subjected
to a higher asylum standard.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:48.900
- Those who cross
illegally and haven't asked

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.190
for protections in other countries

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.560
prior to their arrival here, by and large,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:53.520
won't be eligible.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:55.800
They'll face swift deportation.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:57.120
- [Narrator] And they
will be deported back

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:59.520
to their home countries or back to Mexico,

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.680
which has agreed to keep taking them.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.270
The administration also plans

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:05.370
to open new migrant processing centers

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.850
in Guatemala and Colombia to
create some legal pathways

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.260
for asylum seekers.

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:12.600
Yet it's unclear when
the centers would open

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.060
or how much impact they will have.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.900
- They're also pushing people
to use the CBP One app.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.270
It's an app that you can
make an appointment to come

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.820
to a legal border
crossing, a port of entry,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:27.000
and make your case to
enter the United States.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.980
- [Narrator] Asylum Seekers
at the border will be

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.930
essentially barred from
entering the country

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.700
under the rules, unless they use

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.496
the app's appointment system.

00:04:34.496 --> 00:04:38.829
- (Michael speaks foreign language)

00:04:46.556 --> 00:04:47.670
- If you have a real mix of people

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:51.630
who are trying to use this
app with some success,

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.510
and others saying that they
just can't wait any longer

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.980
in making the track.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.480
The expectation is that a lot

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.150
of people will simply
make the effort to cross

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.016
and see what happens.

00:05:02.016 --> 00:05:06.183
- (Reyna speaks foreign language)

00:05:07.621 --> 00:05:10.649
- (Reporter speaks foreign language)

00:05:10.649 --> 00:05:14.816
- (Reyna speaks foreign language)

00:05:18.545 --> 00:05:20.319
- (Reporter speaks foreign language)

00:05:20.319 --> 00:05:21.402
- (Reyna speaks foreign language)

00:05:21.402 --> 00:05:24.685
- (Reporter speaks foreign language)

00:05:24.685 --> 00:05:26.927
- (Reyna speaks foreign language)

00:05:26.927 --> 00:05:29.510
(bright music)

